 difference.\n\n             Present                        Past\n        B32\n             You  never cook  a meal.       You  never cooked  a meal.\n             I sometimes  watch  a movie.   | sometimes  watched  a movie.\n             We  often phone  our parents.  We  often phoned  our parents.\n        A    Note: If it is difficult to say the -ed ending in words like cooked, imagine that the -ed is joined to the\n             word  after. For example say cooked all the food this: cook tall the food.\n        A    Note: If the word after the past tense verb begins with a consonant, you may not hear the -ed,\n             e.g. cooked dinner, walked through.\n\n\n   62\n                English Pronunciation in Use", "char_count": 2655, "mean_conf": 90.68, "word_count": 320, "words": [{"text": "B30", "x0": 178, "y0": 556, "x1": 246, "y1": 608, "conf": 83, "bold": false}, {"text": "B31", "x0": 173, "y0": 1771, "x1": 225, "y1": 1805, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "B32", "x0": 161, "y0": 2403, "x1": 232, "y1": 2457, "conf": 76, "bold": false}, {"text": "The", "x0": 276, "y0": 306, "x1": 350, "y1": 343, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "verb", "x0": 365, "y0": 307, "x1": 448, "y1": 343, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "play", "x0": 461, "y0": 307, "x1": 543, "y1": 353, "conf": 88, "bold": false}, {"text": "/plet/", "x0": 557, "y0": 308, "x1": 658, "y1": 350, "conf": 77, "bold": false}, {"text": "has", "x0": 671, "y0": 307, "x1": 734, "y1": 345, "conf": 90, "bold": false}, {"text": "one", "x0": 750, "y0": 322, "x1": 817, "y1": 345, "conf": 97, "bold": false}, {"text": "syllable", "x0": 833, "y0": 308, "x1": 974, "y1": 355, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "and", "x0": 989, "y0": 309, "x1": 1060, "y1": 346, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 1075, "y0": 309, "x1": 1132, "y1": 346, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "past", "x0": 1147, "y0": 320, "x1": 1226, "y1": 356, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "tense", "x0": 1240, "y0": 3